<item>
            <title>[LU-20545] Fix inode ref leak on cached  .lustre/fid  open-by-fid</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20545</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;tt&gt;ll_iget_for_nfs()&lt;/tt&gt;, when opening a special FID under &lt;tt&gt;.lustre&lt;/tt&gt;, the code takes an inode reference via &lt;tt&gt;search_inode_for_lustre()&lt;/tt&gt;, then looks up an existing dentry with &lt;tt&gt;d_lookup()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the dentry is already cached, the reference from &lt;tt&gt;search_inode_for_lustre()&lt;/tt&gt; should be dropped, otherwise, each hit of this path leaks one inode ref until the client is unmounted or the inode is forced out some other way.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="98742">LU-20545</key>
